<%# The session-drift browser store (docs/SESSION_DRIFT.md): studio/session, an ES
    module that publishes window.StudioSession and is the default export of
    "studio/session". layouts/studio/_head renders this right below the import
    map, and before Alpine, so the store's alpine:init listener is in place when
    Alpine starts. Its stamp is studio/_session_stamp, higher in the head.

    GUARDED ON THE SAME HELPER AS THE STAMP. studio_session_page_stamp comes from
    Studio::SessionDrift, which Studio::ErrorHandling includes; a head rendered
    anywhere else emits nothing here.

    THE STORE DOES NOT DEPEND ON THE STAMP. A nil stamp omits the meta tag and
    still loads the store, which stays dormant. The tag is Turbo-tracked like
    every engine asset, and Turbo fully reloads when two pages' tracked scripts
    differ, so a page whose stamp failed must not also drop the store and turn
    the next click into a reload. %>
<% if respond_to?(:studio_session_page_stamp) %>
<%= javascript_include_tag "studio/session", type: "module", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
<% end %>
